---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '@/components/layout/Header.astro';
import Footer from '@/components/layout/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About AI Explained"
  description="Why AI Explained exists: practical, evidence-led learning about AI systems for engineers and technical people."
>
  <Header />

  <main class="flex-1 max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-10 sm:py-16">
    <section class="mb-12 sm:mb-16">
      <p class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-brand-400 mb-3">Why this exists</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold text-white mb-5">AI is not magic. It is also not simple.</h1>
      <div class="prose-lesson">
        <p>There is a strange pressure around AI right now. People feel they should already know what MCP, agents, context windows and multi-agent systems mean. So we learn the vocabulary first, then quietly hope nobody asks us to explain the machinery.</p>
        <p>AI Explained is for getting past that. It begins with the automation engineers already understand, then makes each new capability visible: what the model does, what the harness does, what policy permits, which tool creates an effect, and where the evidence lives.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12 sm:mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-5">How we work here</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-3 text-sm">
        {[
          ['Plain English first', 'We introduce the mechanism without assuming the learner is already fluent in the jargon.'],
          ['Build one evolving system', 'The Engineering Troubleshooting Workbench gives every concept somewhere concrete to live.'],
          ['Keep boundaries visible', 'Model output is a proposal. Code, policy, tools, state and events retain their own responsibilities.'],
          ['Treat sources honestly', 'Specifications, established engineering practice, research patterns and vendor implementations are not the same kind of claim.'],
          ['Make failure part of learning', 'A lesson is incomplete if it cannot show what changes when an assumption breaks.'],
        ].map(([title, copy]) => (
          <div class="card py-4 sm:py-5">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-white mb-1">{title}</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">{copy}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12 sm:mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white mb-4">Built by Mohamed Ansari</h2>
      <div class="prose-lesson">
        <p>Mohamed is an Engineering Manager working across AI Platform Engineering, SRE, Observability and DevOps. This guide is shaped by the questions that matter after the demo: What is this system actually doing? What can it touch? How does it fail? Can we observe, explain and improve it?</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm">
        <a href="https://hmohamedansari.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300 transition-colors">Personal site →</a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/mohamedansari/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300 transition-colors">LinkedIn →</a>
        <a href="https://hmohamedansari.github.io/there-is-no-agent-talk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300 transition-colors">There Is No Agent →</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-2xl border border-brand-500/20 bg-brand-950/20 p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-2">This is a living field guide.</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">Protocols and providers move quickly. If something is inaccurate, unclear or missing the part that makes it useful, please say so. The source and curriculum are open for review.</p>
      <a href="https://github.com/hmohamedansari/ai-explained" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex mt-5 text-sm font-medium text-brand-400 hover:text-brand-300 transition-colors">View the source on GitHub →</a>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
